:null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible after #109118\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.beta6 - Arch Linux #1 SMP PREEMPT_DYNAMIC Thu, 11 Sep 2025 17:42:36 +0000 on Wayland - X11 display driver, Single-window, 1 monitor - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - Mesa Intel(R) Graphics (ADL GT2) - 12th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-1235U (12 threads) - 15.35 ГиБ memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nIf DPITexture was rasterized when content scale factor wasn't equal to 1 (or in canvas item scaling mode when window size wasn't equal content size), when used in NinePatchRect, StyleBoxTexture or similar it will be working not very good (see video below). Resetting content scale factor to 1 manually or via window resize fixes issue.\nAlso, if there is any usage except specified (NinePatchRect or StyleBoxTexture), problem is gone\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/dce0c876-cdfb-4198-ad01-9fdfe39bb80a\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Add DPITexture to StyleBoxTexture or NinePatchRect (don't add to anything else!)\n2. Set Content Scale Factor to something greater than 1.0\n3. Run the game, notice texture doesn't get oversampled to specified scale factor\n4. Try to change window size, notice oversampling working differently\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[mrp.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/22309044/mrp.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/g